      "message": "The smaller-access point is right, the driver does write GITS_CWRITER with writel. I think the new test goes the other way though: access_size is the register\u0027s own width from the table, so access_size \u003c\u003d reg_size skips the handler whenever the access matches the register rather than being wider than it, and the loop falls through to pkvm_handle_forward_req.\n\nThat is what the driver does everywhere else. GITS_CTLR and GICR_CTLR via writel, GITS_CBASER, GITS_BASER, GICR_PROPBASER and GICR_PENDBASER via writeq. All of those now reach the hardware unmediated, and only the CWRITER doorbell is still emulated.\n\nCould this be \u003c rather than \u003c\u003d?",
